    fix(factoryState): score-tier citing, uniform auxiliary vocabulary, marked carried records (gh-816 rework threads 2-4)

    - thread 2 (IMPORTANT): among real runs, cite by score tier — the
      machine's own validation workflow (ciWorkflow path match, score 2)
      outranks every bare real run (score 1) however fresh; an unrelated
      repo workflow (labeler/docs/lint — fail-open real under the
      repo-wide runs list) only cites when nothing better exists. The
      residual breadth is now owned in the classifier comment.
    - thread 4: checks.auxiliary drops its private 'state' field and is
      runCite-shaped — verdict/conclusion, one vocabulary across
      cite/auxiliary/carried records; schema note added to the header.
    - thread 3: a merged_recent carried record whose conclusion never
      landed rides marked carried:true — unverified, not live, so a
      merged card can no longer read 'validation in flight' for 24h.
    - tests: new RED-first tests for all three; existing recency-only
      expectations updated to the tightened spec; run_all 2204/0.

