{"content":"## 💡 Thread 3 (SUGGESTION) — carried active records are marked, not live

Fixed in `19e7799f` (`js/factoryState.js`, `merged_recent` builder): when the merge tick falls back to the record carried from the card's open life, a record whose conclusion never landed is tagged:

```js
if (mergedChecks.conclusion == null) mergedChecks.carried = true;
```

- **terminal records carry verbatim** — a resolved verdict is exactly the audit trail the terminal lane exists for (no marker noise);
- **an in-flight record rides marked `carried: true`** — unverified history, never a live verdict, so a merged card can no longer read "validation in flight" for the whole 24h window.

The marker keeps the audit fields uniform (see thread 4 — cite/auxiliary/carried are all one record shape). A resolved fresh cite is never tagged.

**Tests**: `a carried in-flight record rides the merged card marked carried (never reads live)` (runId kept, `carried === true`, `conclusion === null`); the existing carried-terminal and fresh-cite tests now also pin `carried === undefined`.
